lear path to a winning formation with good scoring patterns. The Dots tiles are somewhat scattered (B1-B4 range and B7-B8 range with a gap). Taking Chi B7 would expose another meld, reducing my flexibility and scoring potential (concealed hands score more). With unshown tiles still available, it's better to pass and see what I can draw naturally to build a stronger hand.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
